{
  "heading": "Limited Store and Query",
  "body": "Store names an Entity class from the same source, like Store(ProductEntity, {...}), and at most 64 allowed fields. It is shared behavior, not a dependency injection registration. Bare Store (Store with no arguments) keeps its Yon-only provider meaning. Query methods with an empty body compile to find, count or exists operations. They use either a structured Query or derived names: findByStatus, countByStatus, existsByStatus and the same names in snake_case. Derived predicates (conditions) support Equals, NotEquals, LessThan, LessThanEqual, GreaterThan, GreaterThanEqual, In, IsNull and IsNotNull, joined by And. The structured operators are eq/ne/lt/lte/gt/gte/in/isNull/isNotNull. Tachyon does not accept SQL text, expressions, OR, joins, nested paths or bulk changes. The entity adapter receives a query command with bound values (values sent apart from the query text). The adapter must have authorizeEntity(command, execution). That method must return true before execute runs. The limits are eight predicates, 100 In values, 64 KiB of bindings and 1 MiB of results. Find returns at most the requested page size, and the maximum is 100. The annotation sets the order. When two results have the same order, the ID decides. The caller's page.sort must be empty. Count returns a nonnegative safe integer. Exists returns a boolean. Query cannot combine with other method policies. The examples run queries through an explicit, authorized in-memory adapter. Every language declares the same store and controller route.",
